## Executive Summary

We are building the **memory layer for AI**—the Stripe/Twilio of persistent memory. Every AI application needs memory. Today, developers build it from scratch, use fragmented solutions, or lock into walled gardens. Marrow: **DX-first** (we lead with developer experience), **model-agnostic** (works with any LLM), **compliance built in** (SOC2, GDPR from day one). Our goal: become the standard that model providers and developers use.

---

## The Problem

### 1. AI Has No Memory

- **LLMs are stateless.** Each API call is independent. No continuity across sessions.
- **Context windows are finite.** Even 200k tokens isn't enough for long-term knowledge.
- **Every app reinvents the wheel.** Developers build custom RAG, vector DBs, and retrieval logic.
- **Users repeat themselves.** "My name is Jeff." "I prefer short answers." "I'm building a memory startup." Said in every app, every time.

### 2. Memory Is Fragmented

- **Walled gardens.** ChatGPT remembers you in ChatGPT. Claude remembers you in Claude. Nothing crosses over.
- **No standard.** Every implementation is different. No interoperability. Developers rebuild the same thing every time.

### 3. Compliance Is an Afterthought

- **Enterprise can't adopt** AI memory without SOC2, GDPR, data residency.
- **Developers need** a solution that meets compliance out of the box—not something they build themselves.

### 4. Model Providers Can't Solve This Alone

- OpenAI, Anthropic, Google focus on models. Memory is infrastructure.
- They need a layer that: works with any model, integrates simply, meets compliance.
- Building it in-house is a distraction. Partnering with a standard is the path.

